---
/**
 * Wave-1 spoken page body #1 — IVF & Frozen Embryo Chinese Baby Predictor.
 * EN-only spoke (route registered in EN_ONLY_PATH). All UI strings come from
 * `IVF_STRINGS` / `IVF_FAQ` (src/i18n/tools.ts); editorial prose lives here,
 * matching the site's English-only editorial pattern.
 */
import IvfPredictor from '@components/calculators/IvfPredictor.tsx';
import FaqAccordion from '@theme/components/FaqAccordion.astro';
import RelatedTools from '@theme/components/RelatedTools.astro';
import GeoLeadLinks from '@theme/components/GeoLeadLinks.astro';
import { IVF_STRINGS, IVF_FAQ } from '@i18n/tools';
import { getDictionary } from '@i18n/translations';
import type { Locale } from '@i18n/utils';

interface Props { locale?: Locale; }
const { locale = 'en' } = Astro.props;
const t = getDictionary(locale);
const S = IVF_STRINGS;
---

<div class="pt-10">
  <div class="section-shell grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.05fr]">
    <div>
      <p class="chip mb-4"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-girl-500 to-boy-500"></span>IVF · FET · IUI · Donor egg</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-[2.35rem] font-extrabold leading-[1.1] text-plum-900 sm:text-5xl">
        IVF &amp; Frozen Embryo <span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-girl-500 via-girl-400 to-boy-500 bg-clip-text text-transparent">Chinese Baby Predictor</span> (FET, IUI &amp; Donor)
      </h1>
      <span class="mt-4 block h-1.5 w-16 rounded-full" aria-hidden="true" style="background-image: linear-gradient(to right, var(--color-girl-500), var(--color-boy-500)); box-shadow: 0 4px 10px -3px rgba(221,33,117,.45);"></span>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-plum-600">
        Compare the two moments an IVF baby "begins" — egg retrieval and embryo transfer — on the traditional
        Qing Palace chart at once, with donor-egg readings for both parents-by-intent.
      </p>

      <GeoLeadLinks />
      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="chip"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full" style="background-image:linear-gradient(120deg,#dd2175,#2c63e8)"></span>Free &amp; instant</span>
        <span class="chip"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full" style="background-image:linear-gradient(120deg,#2c63e8,#f59e0b)"></span>Both dates compared</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-8 rounded-3xl p-5" style="border: 1px solid transparent; background: linear-gradient(rgba(253,242,248,.65), rgba(253,242,248,.65)) padding-box, linear-gradient(120deg, rgba(238,90,151,.3), rgba(126,169,249,.3)) border-box;">
        <p class="font-display font-bold text-plum-800">🍼 {t.common.entertainment}</p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-plum-600">
          <strong>IVF chromosomal sex is determined at fertilization by sperm genetics.</strong> If PGT-A
          (preimplantation genetic testing) was performed, clinical lab results are ~99%+ accurate.
          This lunar calculator is an ancient cultural curiosity.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 min-h-[520px]"><IvfPredictor client:idle strings={S} locale={locale} /></div>
  </div>

  <section class="section-shell mt-14">
    <div class="prose-custom">
      <h2>Retrieval Date vs. Transfer Date: Which Moment Does Chinese Astrology Count?</h2>
      <p>
        The traditional chart is read from the <strong>moment of conception</strong>. In a natural pregnancy that is the
        day egg meets sperm. In an IVF cycle that moment happens in the lab: the <strong>egg retrieval date</strong>
        (whether fertilization happens by conventional insemination or ICSI) is the closest Gregorian date to
        conception, while the <strong>embryo transfer date</strong> marks implantation — a biologically meaningful but
        different moment. Traditionalists read the chart from retrieval because the baby's "lunar seed" is
        considered planted when fertilization occurs, and clinics themselves date IVF pregnancies from retrieval
        or LMP rather than from transfer. Our dual-comparison calculator shows both readings side-by-side so you
        never have to guess which one a website silently used.
      </p>
      <h2>How Day-5 Blastocyst Math Shifts the Boundary Dates</h2>
      <p>
        A day-3 embryo is transferred roughly 2 days after retrieval; a day-5/6 blastocyst is transferred
        4–5 days after retrieval. If you only know the transfer date, subtract the embryo's age at transfer to
        reconstruct fertilization — that subtraction can move you across a lunar month boundary, which is exactly
        why two people with the same transfer date can "legitimately" report different chart cells. The calculator's
        fresh-cycle mode performs this embryo-day math for you and flags any split verdict rather than hiding it.
      </p>
      <h2>Donor Egg vs. the Carrying Mother's Energy</h2>
      <p>
        Donor-egg cycles create a genuine folkloric dilemma: the egg carries the <strong>donor's lunar lineage</strong>
        (her age at retrieval selects the chart row), while the womb that incubates the pregnancy belongs to the
        <strong>carrying mother</strong> (her lunar age at transfer). There is no "official" answer inside the tradition —
        practitioners split on it — so our tool computes both readings and lets you compare them instead of
        pretending only one exists.
      </p>
      <h2>Clinical PGT-A Testing vs. Folklore</h2>
      <p>
        Be clear about what this website is and is not. Lunar calendar gender prediction is cultural heritage and
        runs at coin-flip odds in large-scale testing (see the 2010 Swedish registry analysis linked in our trust
        footer). If knowing an IVF baby's sex matters — for X-linked family conditions or family balancing — the
        clinical route is <em>preimplantation genetic testing</em> (PGT-A, which also screens chromosome count), read
        on a blastocyst biopsy. Regulations on elective sex selection vary by country and clinic. For authoritative
        medical context see
        <a href="https://www.sart.org/" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">SART</a> and
        <a href="https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/prenatal-genetic-screening-tests" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">ACOG's prenatal genetic screening FAQ</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-shell mt-14" aria-labelledby="ivf-faq">
    <h2 id="ivf-faq" class="section-title text-center">IVF gender-predictor FAQ</h2>
    <div class="mt-6"><FaqAccordion items={IVF_FAQ} /></div>
  </section>

  <RelatedTools t={t} locale={locale} exclude="chinese-gender-predictor/" />
</div>
